ink><description>周三，月球的阴影席卷了地球，吸引了全球数百万人的目光。这是自 2024 年 4 月北美日食以来的首次日全食</description><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-magnificent-photos-of-the-total-solar-eclipse-over-europe-that-showcase-the-suns-beauty-and-the-wonder-of-skywatching-180989325/</guid></item><item><title>几千年前，丹尼索瓦人可能体型庞大，尤其是与他们的古代人类邻居相比</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/thousands-of-years-ago-denisovans-might-have-been-huge-especially-compared-to-their-archaic-human-neighbors-180989327/</link><description>新的研究为我们生活在亚洲的已灭绝表亲提供了罕见的见解，他们可能比娇小的“直立人”还要高大</description><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 22:14:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/thousands-of-years-ago-denisovans-might-have-been-huge-especially-compared-to-their-archaic-human-neighbors-180989327/</guid></item><item><title>麻省理工学院的一位历史学家发现了这个长期以来被认为是波士顿倾茶事件纪念品的中国标签的惊人真相</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-historian-at-mit-discovered-the-surprising-truth-about-this-chinese-label-long-thought-to-be-a-souvenir-of-the-boston-tea-party-180989328/</link><description>波士顿旧南会议厅展出的文物传奇展示了历史研究的演变</description><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 21:17:23 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-historian-at-mit-discovered-the-surprising-truth-about-this-chinese-label-long-thought-to-be-a-souvenir-of-the-boston-tea-party-180989328/</guid></item><item><title>NASA 完成了航行者 2 号探测器的大胆“大爆炸”修复，使其能够继续研究星际空间</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasa-completes-daring-big-bang-fix-on-the-voyager-2-probe-allowing-it-to-keep-studying-interstellar-space-180989312/</link><description>科学家们将探测器的三个加热装置更换为消耗更少能量的装置，他们可能会对旅行者 1 号做同样的事情。这两个航天器都在大约 50 年前发射</description><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 20:09:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasa-completes-daring-big-bang-fix-on-the-voyager-2-probe-allowing-it-to-keep-studying-